# cabin_fog_far: morning fog in the valley (BUILD_PLAN S7, 5.8): a solid band
# of the vapour's light over its shade (snow over glacier blue by day and at
# dawn, never pink: content/home/cabin.json remaps) over the foothills and
# the peak's foot, its top a row of rounded puffs, its foot a softer row of
# them, one checker row where the two meet; the summit floats over it.
# It parts behind the stovepipe (S7b, Lead call 69): from x 61 to 75 its
# top drops in two rounded puff sides to row 83, just under the pipe's cap,
# so the smoke's column rises against the knoll, as in clear weather, and
# never white on white. Outlined in its own colors, its ends one pixel
# outside the plate (clipped), then filled. On the far layer, at the
# plate's origin.
